        plan("The District Planning Committee", [9], "The four-fifths elected-member rule makes it representative and not a State department.", "Use the correct article and composition rule for district-planning demands."),
        plan("Metropolitan planning and electoral continuity", [10, 11], "Constitution and effectiveness are State-variable and no compliance count exists here.", "Cover the metropolitan and continuity gaps that most answers omit entirely."),
        plan("Scheduled Areas and the consultation limit", [12], "The statute requires consultation before land acquisition and resettlement, not consent.", "Protect a Scheduled-Areas answer from the single commonest legal misstatement."),
        plan("The benchmark case and the three-way distinction", [13, 14], "Attach no percentage to the benchmark and grade the extent rather than answering yes or no.", "Convert an extent demand into a graded finding with a named positive benchmark."),
